  "result": "All 10 tests pass (6 original + 4 new).\n\n- **rotate.sh** \u2014 `rotate.sh --keep N` used `tail -n +\"$keep\"` on the oldest-first archive list, which deleted from the KEEP-th entry onward (the newest); now it deletes the first `total - keep` entries (the oldest) and exits early when `total <= keep`.\n- **verify.sh** \u2014 the sidecar's file name was taken as awk's second field, truncating `my backup-\u2026.tar.gz` at the space and reporting \"archive missing\"; it now splits off only the digest, keeping the full name.\n- **lib/common.sh** (new) \u2014 holds the shared option parser (`parse_options`, with `is_uint`/`need_value`) and `resolve_dir`, with a double-sourcing guard like `lib/log.sh`; sourced by rotate.sh and verify.sh, which accept the same flags as before.\n- **tests/run_tests.sh** \u2014 added a rotate group (exactly-N keeps everything, newest survives, keep-2-of-3 deletes only the oldest) and a verify group for an archive name containing a space.\n\nI changed rotate.sh, verify.sh, and tests/run_tests.sh, and added lib/common.sh.",
